3D Gear Design Using AutoCAD
Project Overview

This project demonstrates the design of a 3D spur gear using AutoCAD. The gear model was created using basic 2D drafting and 3D modeling tools available in AutoCAD.

The purpose of this project is to understand gear geometry, CAD modeling techniques, and mechanical design fundamentals.

Objectives
Design a 3D spur gear in AutoCAD
Learn basic mechanical drafting
Practice 3D modeling commands
Create an accurate gear profile
Software Used
AutoCAD
Windows OS
Gear Specifications
Parameter	Value
Gear Type	Spur Gear
Number of Teeth	20
Module	2 mm
Pressure Angle	20°
Thickness	10 mm

Pitch Circle Diameter Formula:

D=m×Z

Where:

D = Pitch Diameter
m = Module
Z = Number of Teeth
Steps Performed
Created the pitch circle
Designed a single gear tooth
Used Polar Array to duplicate teeth
Converted the 2D sketch into a 3D model using Extrude
Applied finishing and editing tools
AutoCAD Commands Used
Circle
Line
Trim
Polar Array
Extrude
Union
Fillet
Result

The final output is a fully designed 3D spur gear model created in AutoCAD. The project helped improve CAD drafting and 3D modeling skills.

Applications
Mechanical Engineering
Automobile Systems
Robotics
Industrial Machines
Conclusion

This project successfully demonstrates the process of designing a 3D gear using AutoCAD. It provides practical experience in CAD modeling and mechanical component design.3D Gear Design Using AutoCAD
